{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":1118,"output":1112,"cacheRead":10976,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":24,"totalTokens":13206,"cost":{"input":0.0005031,"output":0.0035584,"cacheRead":0.0005488,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0046103}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":2,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ee430b5b469c57d","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# Event projector incident\n\nStatus: resolved\n\n## Impact\n\nThe trade event projector was unusable as a durable pipeline:\n\n- **Lost writes after one store failure.** A single rejected `applyToStore`\n  poisoned the shared promise chain, so every subsequent `project()` call for\n  *any* trade inherited the same rejection and silently stopped making\n  progress.\n- **Global serialization.** One `pending` chain was shared by all trades, so a\n  slow or failing store write for one trade blocked unrelated trades behind it.\n- **No version discipline.** Events were applied in call order with no\n  versioning, so duplicates, stale events, gaps, and events on unknown trades\n  all \"succeeded\".\n- **State could commit on failure and mutate through the API.** `states` was\n  written before `applyToStore` completed, and `AMENDED` payloads were spread\n  into the state object without field-level validation.\n\n## Root cause\n\n1. `project` chained every trade through a single shared promise\n   (`pending = pending.then(...)`). When `applyToStore` rejected, `pending`\n   became a permanently rejected promise, so all later `then(...)` links were\n   skipped and rejected with the stale error — the \"temporary\" failure became\n   permanent, and one trade's failure blocked every other trade.\n2. There was no per-trade event queue, no version validation (first event must\n   be `CREATED` v1, later events exactly current+1, duplicates/stale return\n   the snapshot, gaps reject), no terminal handling for `CANCELLED`, and no\n   payload validation, so malformed input changed state.\n3. State was written to the in-memory map before the persistence call, so a\n   rejected write still left committed-looking state.\n\n## Fix\n\n`event-projector.mjs` was rewritten:\n\n- Per-trade promise chains (`chains` map keyed by `tradeId`) so events for one\n  trade apply serially in call order while different trades progress\n  concurrently.\n- The chain link is detached from the caller-visible result\n  (`result.then(() => undefined, () => undefined)`), so a rejected event never\n  poisons later events for the same trade or another trade.\n- Version discipline: first accepted event must be `CREATED` at version 1;\n  later accepted events must be exactly current version + 1; duplicate/stale\n  versions return a copy of the current snapshot without persisting; version\n  gaps and invalid first events reject (`RangeError`) without changing state.\n- `CANCELLED` is terminal; a later new version rejects.\n- State is committed to the map only after `applyToStore` resolves.\n- `CREATED` requires positive finite `notional` and non-empty `owner`;\n  `AMENDED` may replace either field but must leave a valid complete state;\n  only `CREATED`/`AMENDED`/`CANCELLED` are supported and malformed events\n  reject with `TypeError`.\n- `AMENDED` copies only known fields instead of spreading the raw payload.\n- All inputs passed to the store and all returned states/snapshots are\n  `structuredClone` copies, so external mutation cannot reach internal state.\n\n## Regression coverage\n\n`student-tests.mjs` now contains seven `node:test` cases:\n\n1. Different trades progress concurrently while one trade is blocked in the\n   store (proves no global queue).\n2. Duplicate and stale versions return the current snapshot without persisting.\n3. Version gaps and invalid first events reject without changing state.\n4. A `CANCELLED` trade is terminal.\n5. A store rejection leaves state unchanged and does not block the same trade\n   (retry succeeds) or another trade.\n6. Malformed events and invalid payloads reject with `TypeError` without\n   changing state.\n7. Returned states, snapshots, and store payloads are independent copies.\n\nThese run alongside the committed `event-projector.test.mjs` cases\n(serialization for one trade; a persistence rejection not committing state or\npoisoning later work).\n\n## Remaining risk\n\n- `getSnapshot` accepts any non-throwing `tradeId` lookup and returns `null`\n  for unknown trades; callers must treat `null` as \"no trade\".\n- Persistence is not idempotent at the store layer: a retry of a previously\n  rejected event is resent, which is correct here only because the store\n  failure is assumed fully temporary.\n- Validation covers the documented event shape; exotic inputs (e.g. objects\n  with non-cloneable values) would surface as `structuredClone` errors rather\n  than `TypeError`.\n- Verification was `node --test` on the two fixture test files; the wider\n  `npm run verify` lane was not part of this incident's boundary.\n","path":"benchmark/fixtures/T10-event-projector/INCIDENT.md"}}}}
