{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":299,"output":610,"cacheRead":13328,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":27,"totalTokens":14237,"cost":{"input":0.00013455000000000002,"output":0.0019520000000000002,"cacheRead":0.0006664,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0027529500000000005}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"\n\nAll 9 tests pass (2 committed + 7 student). Done.\n\n## Root cause\n`event-projector.mjs` routed **every trade through one shared promise chain** (`pending = pending.then(...)`). When `applyToStore` rejected, `pending` became permanently rejected, so every later `project()` call for *any* trade skipped its handler and inherited the stale rejection — a temporary failure became permanent and blocked all trades. The code also had no version discipline (duplicates/gaps/invalid first events silently \"applied\"), no `CANCELLED` terminal handling, no payload validation, and committed state before persistence completed.\n\n## Repair (`event-projector.mjs`, rewritten)\n- **Per-trade promise chains** keyed by `tradeId` — one trade is serial in call order; different trades progress concurrently.\n- Chain link detached from the caller-visible promise (`result.then(() => undefined, () => undefined)`), so a rejection never poisons later events for the same or other trades.\n- Version rules: first event must be `CREATED` v1; later events exactly current+1; duplicate/stale versions return a copy of the current snapshot without persisting; gaps and invalid first events reject (`RangeError`) with no state change; `CANCELLED` is terminal.\n- State commits to the map only **after** `applyToStore` resolves.\n- `CREATED` requires positive finite `notional` and non-empty `owner`; `AMENDED` replaces only known fields and must leave a valid complete state; unsupported/malformed events reject with `TypeError`.\n- All store payloads, returned states, and snapshots are `structuredClone` copies.\n\n## Tests added (`student-tests.mjs`, 7 cases)\n1. Trades progress concurrently while one trade is blocked in the store (no global queue)\n2. Duplicate/stale versions return the snapshot without persisting\n3. Version gaps and invalid first events reject without changing state\n4. `CANCELLED` trade is terminal\n5. A store rejection leaves state unchanged and doesn't block the same trade (retry succeeds) or another trade\n6. Malformed events/payloads reject with `TypeError` without changing state\n7. Returned states/snapshots/store payloads are immutable copies\n\n## Visible result\n```\nℹ tests 9\nℹ pass 9\nℹ fail 0\n```\n\n## Remaining risk\n- Retries resend the same event; correctness relies on the store failure being fully temporary (no store-side idempotency guarantees).\n- Exotic inputs with non-cloneable values would surface as `structuredClone` errors rather than `TypeError`.\n- Verification was scoped to the two fixture test files; the broader `npm run verify` lane was outside this task's boundary."}}
